# 15 — Appendix: every script, and every artifact

## Scripts

{{n_scripts}} scripts, {{n_script_lines}} lines. Four of them exit non-zero on
`--help` **on purpose** — two print a usage block because they take positional
directories, one needs a release, and one **refuses to run at all** because it
is a phase-1 schema patch and would downgrade the schema from
{{schema_version}}. The test that covers the sweep greps for a traceback
rather than checking exit codes, for exactly that reason.

{{script_table}}

## Artifacts

{{n_results_files}} files in `data/results/`, every one stamped with the
content hashes of the graph it was computed from and the commit that computed
it. {{n_refused_results}} is a recorded refusal.

{{results_table}}

## The constants, and where each one is decided

| constant | value | decided by |
|:---|---:|:---|
| `inactive_above_nm` | {{inactive_above_nm}} nM | **measured** from the censored-bound census |
| `active_below_nm` | {{active_below_nm}} nM | a decision about the task, not derived |
| `dose_series_policy` | `{{dose_series_default}}` | fix-list L10, recorded with both branches runnable |
| ECFP4 | radius {{fp_radius}}, {{fp_bits}} bits | `kgav.similarity`, one definition |
| `CHANCE` | {{chance}} | `kgav.calibration` — imported by the agent, never respelled |
| `MIN_REACHED_POSITIVES` | {{min_reached_positives}} | matches the minimum class size the hard-negative script requires |
| landscape `ALPHA` | {{landscape_alpha}} | `kgav.landscape`, imported by the agent so one answer cannot carry two alphas |
| `hub_degree_cut` | {{hub_cut_degree}} | the `Protein` p99.9 on this release |
| `THIN_ROUTE` | {{agent_thin_route}} | not a cutoff: the route is used either way and the number is stated |
| `SI_THRESHOLD` | {{agent_si_threshold}} | the conventional selectivity floor, applied as a report rather than a filter |

