## The floors that make an imputed AUC readable

For the plate-matched cell, the degree baseline reaches
{{hn_degree_cov}} of the positives so its floor is {{hn_degree_floor}} —
exactly chance — and its skill is {{hn_degree_skill}}. The ensemble reaches
{{hn_combined_cov}}, so its floor is {{hn_combined_floor}} and its skill is
{{hn_combined_skill}}. Those two floors are the whole difference between the
two AUCs, which sit {{hn_combined_auc}} and {{hn_degree_auc}}.

## Every registration

{{n_registrations}} documents in `registrations/`, each signed before the
result it governs existed, each amended by appending. The subject is read out
of each file's own title line, so a registration added to the directory
appears here without anyone editing this table — the predecessor of this
index was hand-written, and a registration added without an edit to it was
simply absent.

{{registration_table}}
